1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Dark matter may have just hit a detector. Once.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Not a discovery. Here is what was actually seen

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,500
One nuclear recoil at 248 keV

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,000
220 live days, 2.84 tonne-years of exposure

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Known backgrounds make such an event about 0.5% of the time

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
2.6 sigma global, 3.4 local. Far short of discovery

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,500
If a WIMP, its mass is above 200 GeV

8
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:37,000
A preprint on arXiv. Not yet peer-reviewed

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
One event. Interesting. Not a discovery
